        "original_id": "059f6238-53b3-5c7c-b61b-5a85cdeb36bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wright brothers, Orville Wright, Wilbur Wright, Grant Morton\n- Products: Wright Model B, first successful airplane\n- Places: United States, Venice, California\n- Concepts: aviation pioneers, parachuting\n\nFacts:\n- Orville Wright and Wilbur Wright were American brothers, inventors, and aviation pioneers who are generally credited with inventing, building, and flying the world's first successful airplane.\n- The Wright Model B was an early pusher biplane designed by the Wright brothers in the United States in 1910.\n- Grant Morton, described as a veteran career parachutist, supposedly made the first dive by jumping from a Wright Model B over Venice, California, at age 54.",
